    "growth_divergence_warning": "Equity CAGR (10.9% 5yr) diverges >30% from revenue (3.9%) and EPS (-2.7%) CAGRs. Book value grew on retained earnings and the 2025 Elo acquisition, while FY20->FY25 EPS fell across a full destock cycle; equity CAGR is not a usable growth proxy for a cyclical repurchaser.",
    "notes": "FCF CAGRs are on the owner-FCF series (reported FCF - SBC): FY20 $836M, FY22 $317M, FY25 $656M. The 3yr figure starts at the FY22 trough and is not a growth rate; the 5yr owner-FCF CAGR (-4.7%) is below reported (-1.5%) because SBC rose from $59M to $175M (1.3% -> 3.2% of revenue) -- an increasing share of reported cash flow is being paid in stock. All endpoints are FY2020/FY2022/FY2025 annual rows of ZBRA_Metrics.csv."
  },
  "scenario_narratives": {
    "base": "Refresh cycle and Elo integration carry FY27 to +6%, then growth settles into management's 5-7% organic band and fades to 3% by FY34. Adjusted EBITDA margin returns from the FY26 guided 23.75% peak to a 22.5% mid-cycle level as tariff tailwinds and volume leverage normalise. SBC 3.1% of revenue gliding to 2.6%; cash tax ramps 20% -> 21%.",
    "bull": "Machine vision (Photoneo, Matrox), RFID tagging mandates and the Frontline AI Suite turn Zebra into a software-enabled automation platform: growth 9% fading to 3.5%, adjusted EBITDA 25.5% on software mix and completed tariff mitigation, exit multiple 16x owner FCF.",
    "bear": "The FY26 beat is a channel pull-forward: distributors destock as in FY22-23 (revenue -21% then), FY27 revenue -10% with adjusted EBITDA margin at 19%, recovering only to 21% as tariffs return and low-cost Asian entrants and smartphone/vision-based capture press on pricing; 12x exit."
  },
  "valuation_philosophy": {
    "summary": "Cyclical enterprise-hardware compounder valued on unlevered owner FCF (SBC fully expensed, share count flat) through a mid-cycle margin lens: the FY26 guided peak is the starting point, not the run-rate. Cyclicality is charged in the bear flows and weight, not in the discount rate.",
    "key_risks_to_valuation": [
      "Channel destock: ~50% of sales via ScanSource, BlueStar and Ingram Micro; FY22-23 showed a -21% revenue swing",
      "Peak-margin extrapolation: FY26 adjusted EBITDA 23.5-24.0% includes tariff-mitigation and volume leverage that may not persist",
      "Refinancing: $2,275M of debt is current at 2026-07-04",
      "Tariff regime changes; the ~$73M IEEPA refund is excluded",
      "Equity-award withholding taxes not disclosed in XBRL after FY2021, so house SBC may be understated by up to ~$30M/yr"
    ]
  },
